WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.679
MCP provides a structured way for AI applications to connect with tools, resources, prompts,

00:00:05.679 --> 00:00:06.875
data, and services.

00:00:06.875 --> 00:00:12.853
It helps separate the AI host experience from the integration details of each external system.

00:00:12.853 --> 00:00:16.439
The core architecture involves hosts, clients, servers, capabilities, context,

00:00:16.439 --> 00:00:17.635
and interaction flow.

00:00:17.635 --> 00:00:23.613
Understanding those roles makes it easier to reason about what the AI application can discover,

00:00:23.613 --> 00:00:28.793
what it can read, what it can call, and what it can change.

00:00:28.793 --> 00:00:31.981
Tools, resources, and prompts are different capability types.

00:00:31.981 --> 00:00:33.576
Tools perform defined operations.

00:00:33.576 --> 00:00:36.365
Resources provide data or content as context.

00:00:36.365 --> 00:00:38.358
Prompts provide reusable interaction patterns.

00:00:38.358 --> 00:00:42.343
Capability discovery lets a client learn what a server offers,

00:00:42.343 --> 00:00:47.524
but discovery does not automatically mean every capability should be trusted or enabled.

00:00:47.524 --> 00:00:49.516
Clear descriptions, narrow scope, documentation,

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:54.299
and traceability help users and operators understand how capabilities are being used.

00:00:54.299 --> 00:00:58.682
Useful MCP adoption depends on identity-aware access and careful data handling.

00:00:58.682 --> 00:01:02.269
User identity, application identity, service identity, delegated access, consent,

00:01:02.269 --> 00:01:05.856
least privilege, and tenant boundaries all shape safe use.

00:01:05.856 --> 00:01:09.442
Prompt data, retrieved resources, tool results, logs, cached content,

00:01:09.442 --> 00:01:13.029
and memory features need data minimization, provenance, retention rules,

00:01:13.029 --> 00:01:14.224
and trust-boundary analysis.

00:01:14.224 --> 00:01:19.007
MCP does not remove the need for application security, authorization, privacy review,

00:01:19.007 --> 00:01:20.202
or operational discipline.

00:01:20.202 --> 00:01:24.586
The goal is to make AI integrations more consistent, understandable, auditable,

00:01:24.586 --> 00:01:25.383
and maintainable.

00:01:25.383 --> 00:01:30.564
Good MCP programs define use cases, inventory servers and tools, monitor important events,

00:01:30.564 --> 00:01:34.150
review dependencies, document ownership, and prepare for incident response.

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:38.933
MCP should make external capabilities easier to govern, not harder to see.

00:01:38.933 --> 00:01:43.316
When teams treat it as architecture rather than a novelty feature,

00:01:43.316 --> 00:01:47.700
they can adopt it with clearer control and less operational surprise.
